{"id":"smith_calf_raise","name":"Smith calf raise on a step","cue":"Sink into a deep stretch, pause, and stay in the bottom half.","research":"Standing calf raise on a Smith machine (science audit table B: the Smith calf raise on a step as an alternative to the standing calf raise machine; the bottom half, the long-length partial, grew the gastrocnemius about twice as much as full range, Kassiano 2023). Bar across the upper back (the trapezius point of the Smith squat, skin 0.005 H under the bar), hands 0.26 H each side, vertical rails 0.36 H out at the trap point, plates outboard; a step 0.055 H tall under the bar, the forefoot on its edge with the toe-joint line pinned to the edge so the foot rolls about the metatarsal heads and the toes stay flat; legs straight (knee 3), trunk upright (a lean back of at most 0.3 deg per key keeps the trap point on the rail line). Range as the standing calf raise: ankle 25 deg dorsiflexion (heels below the step top, 0.0105 H clear of the floor plate at the stretch) to 3 deg plantarflexion, 1.5 s pause in the stretch; the bar rises 0.046 H (8 cm). The foot and ankle keys are the standing calf raise sibling and its step fit (0.002 H up). Muscles: the calves (the gastrocnemius, straight knees).","targets":{"tol":10,"A":{"trunk_flexion":0,"knee_flexion":3,"ankle_dorsiflexion":25},"B":{"trunk_flexion":0,"knee_flexion":3,"ankle_dorsiflexion":-3}},"muscles":{"primary":["gastroc"],"secondary":[],"side":"both"},"camera":{"az":110,"el":0,"dAz":0,"dEl":3,"fill":0.6,"note":"Research view az 110 / el 3 (the calves from behind and the right, square to the ankle action). The near rail and plate stand beside the hips and the upper back, above the calves, which are unobstructed from the stretch to the top."},"rhythm":false,"motion":{"tempo":[1,0.2,2,1.5],"root":[0,0.54,-0.096],"base":{"pelvis":{"flex":0},"lumbar":{"flex":1},"thorax":{"flex":1},"neck":{"flex":-8},"head":{"flex":-3},"thigh_l":{"flex":3,"abd":2},"shank_l":{"flex":3},"hand_l":{"pro":9